{
  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_009 (multimodal, scvi_n200, vit_l, concat) achieves 0.532 acc, only ~1.2% above RNA-only (config_003, 0.520), while image-only (config_002) is very weak at 0.227. This suggests the image modality contributes a small signal that may be underutilized by the current concat fusion. Question: config_024 is identical to config_009 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, providing a clean single-variable A/B test of whether the fusion strategy can amplify the image contribution. Why this is the best next experiment: it isolates the fusion effect without confounding changes to encoder, profile setting, or aggregation. If weighted fusion meaningfully improves accuracy, it reveals that fusion design is a lever worth further exploration (and justifies testing other fusion variants). If it does not, it strengthens the hypothesis that the image signal is inherently limited under singleprofile, redirecting effort toward multiprofile or alternative encoders. Under a limited budget, this minimal-change comparison maximizes information per experiment about a key design decision."
}

